`_install_module_batch` calls `module_installer->install($modules, FALSE)` — this calls `install()`, which in turn calls `enable()`. The module_installer->install method is as follows:

```php
public function install(array $modules, $enable_dependencies = TRUE, $notify = TRUE) {
  ...
  $modules = array_filter($modules, [$this, 'isInstallable']);
  ...
  $this->installModules($modules, $enable_dependencies);
  ...
}
```

And `installModules` runs the following:
```php
protected function installModules(array $modules, $enable_dependencies = TRUE) {
  // If the module does not exist, we cannot install it.
  ...
  // Find all dependencies.
  $dependencies = $this->checkRequirements($modules, 'install', $enable_dependencies);
  ...
  $modules = array_merge($modules, $dependencies);
  ...
  $this->enableModules($modules);
  ...
}
```

So the batch installs `$modules` (the group), and then additionally adds the dependencies of those modules. The `geocoder:geocoder` dependency should be pulled in by `openculturas_openstreetmap`. But `openculturas_openstreetmap` isn't in any group…

